"]}, \\\"coverage\\\": {\\\"named_sources_count\\\": 4, \\\"org_citations_count\\\": 4, \\\"data_points_count\\\": 0, \\\"direct_quotes_count\\\": 0, \\\"vague_sources_count\\\": 0, \\\"specificity_ratio\\\": 1.0}, \\\"framing\\\": {\\\"connotation_score\\\": 22.5, \\\"keyword_emphasis_score\\\": 0.0, \\\"omission_score\\\": 40.0, \\\"headline_body_divergence\\\": 52.6, \\\"has_cluster_context\\\": true}}\""}]}}, {"article": {"id": "6547e8bd-cee9-45aa-88f3-95f43cdbf4bf", "title": "Karnataka: CM Shivakumar to hijack NICE project via benami firms; Minister Kumaraswamy vows to expose with evidence", "url": "https://organiser.org/2026/08/25/376940/politics/karnataka-cm-shivakumar-to-hijack-nice-project-via-benami-firms-minister-kumaraswamy-vows-to-expose-with-evidence/", "summary": "Bengaluru: Union Minister H.D. Kumaraswamy on August 25, Tuesday levelled serious allegations against Chief Minister D.K. Shivakumar, claiming that the CM was attempting to take over the NICE (Nandi Infrastructure Corridor Enterprise) project through benami companies. Addressing reporters at the JD(S) office, Kumaraswamy alleged that thousands of acres acquired from farmers for the Bangalore-Mysore Infrastructure Corridor (BMIC) project were at the centre of a larger land-related controversy. He said he would produce documents to substantiate his allegations in the coming week. “According to the information I have, the present Chief Minister is trying to acquire the NICE company through benami companies. Is there one law for farmers and another for the Chief Minister? Thousands of acres acquired in the name of the BMIC project are being targeted. I am not making these allegations merely for a political speech. I will come before the people next week with documents,” Kumaraswamy said...", "published_at": "2026-08-25 11:00:50+00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Organiser", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://organiser.org"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 90, "sensationalism": 2